   $q$Read the sentence: "The archivists faced a difficult choice, restore the faded map or scan it exactly as it was." Which revision is punctuated correctly?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The archivists faced a difficult choice. Restore the faded map or scan it exactly as it was.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unintended-command"},{"text":"The archivists faced a difficult choice: restore the faded map or scan it exactly as it was.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The archivists faced: a difficult choice, restore the faded map or scan it exactly as it was.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"colon-after-verb"},{"text":"The archivists faced a difficult choice; restore the faded map or scan it exactly as it was.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"semicolon-before-fragment"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The archivists faced a difficult choice: restore the faded map or scan it exactly as it was.$q$, $q$The first clause is complete, and what follows spells out the choice, so a colon is the right mark. A semicolon would require a full independent clause after it, and "restore the faded map or scan it" is not one here.$q$, 'draft', null)
