   $q$Which sentence correctly punctuates the coordinate adjectives describing the hike?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The hikers faced a long, steep climb to the old fire tower.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The hikers faced a long steep, climb to the old fire tower.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-before-noun"},{"text":"The hikers faced a, long steep climb to the old fire tower.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-after-article"},{"text":"The hikers faced a long, steep, climb to the old fire tower.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-before-noun"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The hikers faced a long, steep climb to the old fire tower.$q$, $q$"Long" and "steep" each describe the climb equally and could be joined by "and," so a comma separates them. No comma ever goes between the last adjective and the noun it modifies.$q$, 'draft', null)
