   $q$Read the sentence: "The relay team in fact broke its own school record at the spring meet." Which revision correctly sets off the interrupting phrase?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The relay team, in fact, broke its own school record at the spring meet.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The relay team in fact, broke its own school record at the spring meet.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"missing-opening-comma"},{"text":"The relay team, in fact broke its own school record at the spring meet.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"missing-closing-comma"},{"text":"The relay team; in fact, broke its own school record at the spring meet.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"semicolon-for-comma"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The relay team, in fact, broke its own school record at the spring meet.$q$, $q$"In fact" interrupts the sentence between the subject and the verb, so it needs a comma on each side. Using only one comma leaves the interruption half marked.$q$, 'draft', null)
