   $q$Which sentence about desert plants is punctuated correctly?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Many desert plants store water in thick leaves, for example, the aloe can hold moisture for weeks.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-splice"},{"text":"Many desert plants store water in thick leaves; for example the aloe can hold moisture for weeks.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"missing-comma-after-transition"},{"text":"Many desert plants store water in thick leaves: for example; the aloe can hold moisture for weeks.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"semicolon-misplaced"},{"text":"Many desert plants store water in thick leaves; for example, the aloe can hold moisture for weeks.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Many desert plants store water in thick leaves; for example, the aloe can hold moisture for weeks.$q$, $q$Two independent clauses are joined by the transitional phrase "for example," so a semicolon goes before it and a comma after it. Commas alone on both sides create a comma splice.$q$, 'draft', null)
