   $q$Which sentence about the orchard introduces its examples correctly?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The orchard grows several heirloom fruits, such as; quinces, medlars, and pawpaws.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"semicolon-before-list"},{"text":"The orchard grows several heirloom fruits, such as quinces, medlars, and pawpaws.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The orchard grows several heirloom fruits including: quinces, medlars, and pawpaws.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"colon-after-including"},{"text":"The orchard grows several heirloom fruits such as: quinces, medlars, and pawpaws.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"colon-after-such-as"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The orchard grows several heirloom fruits, such as quinces, medlars, and pawpaws.$q$, $q$"Such as" already introduces the examples, so no colon follows it, and a comma before "such as" sets off the nonessential examples. A colon placed after "such as" or "including" interrupts an unfinished phrase.$q$, 'draft', null)
