   $q$Read the sentence: "The decision to move the regional chess finals to the larger library pleased most of the players." Which version is punctuated correctly?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The decision to move the regional chess finals to the larger library, pleased most of the players.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-between-subject-verb"},{"text":"The decision, to move the regional chess finals to the larger library pleased most of the players.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-splits-subject"},{"text":"The decision to move the regional chess finals to the larger library pleased most of the players.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The decision to move the regional chess finals, to the larger library, pleased most of the players.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"commas-around-essential-phrase"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The decision to move the regional chess finals to the larger library pleased most of the players.$q$, $q$The long subject "The decision to move the regional chess finals to the larger library" is one unit, and no comma separates a subject from its verb. A comma after "library" is tempting because of the length, but it breaks the subject from "pleased."$q$, 'draft', null)
