   $q$Read the sentence: "The ticket booth will hand a free program to ___ arrives first on opening night." Which choice correctly completes the sentence?$q$, $q$[{"text":"whose","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"possessive-for-subject"},{"text":"whom","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"object-of-preposition-trap"},{"text":"whoever","is_correct":true},{"text":"whomever","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"object-of-preposition-trap"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$whoever$q$, $q$The pronoun is the subject of the verb "arrives" inside the clause, so it takes the subject form "whoever." The whole clause is the object of "to," which tempts writers to choose "whomever," but the case comes from the pronoun's job inside its own clause.$q$, 'draft', null)
