   $q$Read the sentence: "Beneath the floorboards of the old schoolhouse ___ a bundle of letters and a faded class photograph." Which choice correctly completes the sentence?$q$, $q$[{"text":"is","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"inverted-order-singular"},{"text":"was","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"inverted-order-singular"},{"text":"were","is_correct":true},{"text":"has been","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"inverted-order-singular"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$were$q$, $q$In this inverted sentence the subject comes after the verb: "a bundle of letters and a faded class photograph," two items joined by "and," so the plural "were" is correct. "Was" treats the subject as if it were only the bundle of letters or the word "schoolhouse."$q$, 'draft', null)
