insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('2e5ad929-7059-5093-8ed0-e0c002f6f1ec', 'wg12-narrative-writing-p01', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g12-narrative-writing'), null,
        '9-12', $q$The Rebuttal$q$, $q$(1) The final round of the regional debate tournament was held in the school auditorium, and the stage lights were so bright that I could not see a single face in the audience. (2) My partner, Priya Raman, and I had argued the same side of the same resolution six times that weekend: that our city should keep its public libraries open until midnight. (3) We had won five of those rounds, but the team across the stage had won all six. (4) Their first speaker, a calm junior named Elias Okafor, opened with a statistic about late-night library use that I had never seen before.

(5) I scribbled notes so fast that my pen tore through the paper. (6) Priya slid a folded card across the table. (7) It said, "He's citing a study about a different city." (8) The auditorium was built in 1962 and holds about nine hundred people.

(9) I stood up for the rebuttal with my hands shaking. (10) I explained, as evenly as I could, that the study came from a city three times our size with a completely different bus system. (11) Then I asked the judges to look at our own city's numbers, which we had gathered by visiting branches and counting visitors after eight o'clock. (12) Elias nodded slowly while I spoke, as if he were taking the point seriously.

(13) The judges voted two to one for the other team. (14) We lost.$q$, 'draft')
