   $q$The writer wants to slow the pacing between sentence 9 and sentence 10 to show the narrator's nerves. Which sentence should be added there?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Elias had won a tournament the previous spring, and his partner had won one the year before.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"shifts-focus-from-narrator"},{"text":"Debaters usually have about four minutes to deliver a rebuttal speech in the final round.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"adds-unrelated-fact"},{"text":"Later that evening, my family asked me how the tournament had gone, and I told them everything.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"jumps-ahead-in-time"},{"text":"For a moment the lights blurred, and I heard my own voice before I realized I had started talking.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$For a moment the lights blurred, and I heard my own voice before I realized I had started talking.$q$, $q$The correct sentence stays inside the narrator's experience and stretches a few seconds of nerves. The sentence about the family jumps forward in time instead of slowing the moment.$q$, 'draft', '2e5ad929-7059-5093-8ed0-e0c002f6f1ec')
