   $q$Which revision of sentences 13 and 14 best uses dialogue to give the narrative a stronger ending?$q$, $q$[{"text":"I asked Mr. Delgado about displaying the letters, and he agreed, and then I went home.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"removes-dialogue"},{"text":"\"She kept writing for four years,\" I told Mr. Delgado. \"People should read her.\" He handed me the key to the display case.","is_correct":true},{"text":"\"Clara Voss was born in the nineteenth century,\" I said, and Mr. Delgado wrote that down.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"dialogue-off-point"},{"text":"\"Can the society display the letters?\" I asked. \"Yes,\" Mr. Delgado said. \"Yes, it can.\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"dialogue-without-development"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$"She kept writing for four years," I told Mr. Delgado. "People should read her." He handed me the key to the display case.$q$, $q$The correct choice uses the narrator's words to show why Clara matters and ends with an action that answers the request. The first choice uses dialogue but only repeats a yes, adding nothing about the characters.$q$, 'draft', '4fcac98b-d0a9-5bea-94f7-a57ba1c483af')
