   $q$The writer wants to add a sentence after sentence 9 that links the second paragraph to the third. Which choice best accomplishes this goal?$q$, $q$[{"text":"These measurements, gathered layer by layer, form the evidence that has changed how scientists think about climate.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The hollow drill must be kept cold so that the ice does not crack as it rises to the surface.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"looks-back-only"},{"text":"Future drilling projects hope to reach ice that is more than a million years old.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"introduces-new-topic"},{"text":"The artists who visit the stations often display their paintings in museums back home.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"extends-irrelevant-detail"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$These measurements, gathered layer by layer, form the evidence that has changed how scientists think about climate.$q$, $q$The correct choice refers back to the laboratory measurements and points forward to the climate findings that open paragraph 3, so it bridges the two. The sentence about keeping the drill cold only adds another collection detail and does not lead into the results.$q$, 'draft', '8beec191-b859-51a7-8676-a528d1bb4567')
