   $q$What relationship does the word "however" in sentence 2 signal?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It signals that the writer disagrees with people who find the sport familiar.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-contrast-as-rebuttal"},{"text":"It contrasts the familiar equipment described in sentence 1 with the rules that make the sport different.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It shows that the adapted rules are the cause of the identical court and ball sizes.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-cause-effect"},{"text":"It introduces an example of a rule that the standing game and wheelchair game share.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-contrast-as-example"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It contrasts the familiar equipment described in sentence 1 with the rules that make the sport different.$q$, $q$Sentence 1 stresses what is the same as the standing game, and sentence 2 turns to what is different, the adapted rules, so "however" marks that contrast. It does not signal disagreement with readers, since sentence 1 accepts that the sport looks familiar.$q$, 'draft', '9c94246b-d7fc-59a8-9300-55ce6b37545e')
