-- Passage wg12-paragraph-transitions-p05
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('24fcdd2b-01cc-5a91-8581-0853e5b82979', 'wg12-paragraph-transitions-p05', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g12-paragraph-transitions'), null,
        '9-12', $q$The Quiet Craft of Subtitles$q$, $q$(1) Viewers rarely notice good subtitles, which is exactly what translators hope for. (2) A subtitle must convey what a character says in a limited space, usually no more than two short lines at the bottom of the screen. (3) ____, translators often cut words and condense phrases, since most people cannot read as quickly as actors speak.

(4) Jokes and wordplay present an especially difficult challenge. (5) A pun that depends on two meanings of a word in one language rarely works when it is translated word for word. (6) ____, a translator may replace the original joke with a different one that produces a similar laugh. (7) Some critics argue that this approach changes the film too much, but supporters reply that a joke nobody understands is no longer a joke.

(8) Timing matters as much as wording. (9) Each subtitle has to appear when the character begins speaking and disappear before the scene cuts away, or viewers lose track of who is talking. (10) Translators work with software that displays the sound wave of the dialogue, so they can match each line to the exact moment it is spoken. (11) Some film festivals also award prizes for the best costume design. (12) ____, the best subtitles let viewers forget they are reading at all, so that their attention stays on the story.$q$, 'draft')
on conflict (id) do update set title = excluded.title, body = excluded.body
where public.passages.status = 'draft';
