   $q$Read the sentence: "Each and every volunteer at the food bank received a handwritten note of thanks." Which revision is the most concise?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Every volunteer at the food bank received a handwritten note of thanks.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Each and every single volunteer at the food bank received a handwritten note of thanks.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"redundancy-added"},{"text":"Some volunteers at the food bank received a handwritten note of thanks.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"changes-meaning"},{"text":"Each volunteer and every helper at the food bank received a handwritten note of thanks.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"redundancy-remains"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Every volunteer at the food bank received a handwritten note of thanks.$q$, $q$"Each and every" says the same thing twice, so "Every" alone is enough. "Some volunteers" is short, but it changes how many people received notes.$q$, 'draft', null)
