   $q$A sports columnist wants to praise a chess player who refused to give up in a long, difficult match. Which word best completes the sentence "Even after losing her queen, Adaeze remained ______ and fought her way to a draw."?$q$, $q$[{"text":"obstinate","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-connotation"},{"text":"tenacious","is_correct":true},{"text":"complacent","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-meaning"},{"text":"hardheaded","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-connotation"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$tenacious$q$, $q$"Tenacious" means persistent in a determined, admirable way, which fits praise. "Obstinate" also means refusing to give up, but it suggests unreasonable stubbornness, which undercuts the praise.$q$, 'draft', null)
