   $q$A paragraph reads: "After months of failed trials, the team adjusted the nozzle angle, recalibrated the sensors, and ran the engine test again." The writer wants a short final sentence that emphasizes that the engine fired cleanly. Which choice does this best?$q$, $q$[{"text":"This time, the engine fired cleanly, and the team celebrated with a party.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"adds-new-fact"},{"text":"This time, the engine, after all of the many adjustments that the team had made over months, fired cleanly.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"buries-emphasis"},{"text":"This time, the engine fired cleanly.","is_correct":true},{"text":"This time, the engine fired somewhat cleanly, more or less.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"needless-hedging"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$This time, the engine fired cleanly.$q$, $q$A short sentence after a long one creates contrast and lands the result with force. The long version repeats details the reader already knows and buries the key point in the middle.$q$, 'draft', null)
