   $q$Read the sentence: "The radio telescope collects faint signals from distant galaxies, astronomers analyze the data for months." Which revision fixes the comma splice?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The radio telescope collects faint signals from distant galaxies astronomers analyze the data for months.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"fused-sentence"},{"text":"The radio telescope collects faint signals from distant galaxies, and astronomers analyze the data for months.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The radio telescope collects faint signals from distant galaxies, astronomers then analyze the data for months.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-splice-unfixed"},{"text":"The radio telescope collects faint signals from distant galaxies, however astronomers analyze the data for months.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"conjunctive-adverb-with-comma-only"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The radio telescope collects faint signals from distant galaxies, and astronomers analyze the data for months.$q$, $q$A comma followed by the coordinating conjunction "and" correctly joins two independent clauses. Adding "then" or "however" after the comma still leaves two independent clauses joined by a comma alone, so the splice remains.$q$, 'draft', null)
