   $q$Which sentence should replace sentence 2 so that the draft opens with a clear claim that its evidence supports?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Concrete seawalls have been built along many shorelines for more than a hundred years.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"off-topic-fact"},{"text":"Okafor's experiment suggests that oyster reefs protect a marsh better than a seawall because they absorb wave energy.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Okafor's report is mainly about salt marshes and the different animals that depend on them for food.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"topic-not-claim"},{"text":"Every coastal town should tear down its seawalls this year and replace them with oyster reefs.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opinion-not-analysis"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Okafor's experiment suggests that oyster reefs protect a marsh better than a seawall because they absorb wave energy.$q$, $q$Sentences 3 through 9 compare how the seawall and the reefs handled waves, so a claim that reefs protect better by absorbing wave energy fits the evidence. The choice about what the report is about names a topic but makes no point that evidence could prove.$q$, 'draft', 'aa188600-a618-5070-b6ce-b986ea6b4591')
