   $q$Which revision of sentence 12 would best conclude the draft?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Every bridge in the country should install sensors as soon as possible to prevent accidents.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralization"},{"text":"Bridges are some of the most impressive structures that engineers have ever designed.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"off-topic-opinion"},{"text":"Haddad's evidence shows that sensors are most useful when they guide skilled inspectors rather than replace them.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Haddad's article explains how forty sensors were attached to the Kessel River Bridge in 2020.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"summary-not-analysis"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Haddad's evidence shows that sensors are most useful when they guide skilled inspectors rather than replace them.$q$, $q$The best conclusion ties both paragraphs together: the cracked bearing shows the sensors' value, and the false alarms show why people must decide. The summary choice only repeats a fact from sentence 1 without stating what the evidence shows.$q$, 'draft', '90aee6ac-600b-53b0-917e-2e2927ad6d83')
