   $q$Which sentence should the writer remove, and why?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Sentence 10, because admitting another possible cause weakens the writer's argument.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"avoids-counterclaim"},{"text":"Sentence 9, because a personal story about one purchase is not evidence from Bakr's report.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Sentence 8, because a second statistic distracts from the shop hours.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"removes-key-evidence"},{"text":"Sentence 2, because describing the stalls has nothing to do with the claim.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"removes-needed-context"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Sentence 9, because a personal story about one purchase is not evidence from Bakr's report.$q$, $q$Sentence 9 is an anecdote from outside the text and says nothing about how residents view the street. Sentence 10 should stay, because naming the apartment building lets sentence 11 answer it.$q$, 'draft', 'c1b0f55b-26fe-5cb1-a767-e8fc11297af6')
