   $q$How does sentence 10 affect the writer's argument?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It shows that Faleolo's results are unreliable and should be set aside entirely.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overreads-limitation"},{"text":"It adds further evidence that north winds help dragonflies travel farther.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misidentifies-evidence"},{"text":"It introduces a new claim about where receiving towers ought to be built.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-purpose"},{"text":"It admits the study's limits, which makes the qualified conclusion in sentence 12 more credible.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It admits the study's limits, which makes the qualified conclusion in sentence 12 more credible.$q$, $q$By noting the small sample and limited tracking, the writer shows awareness of what the data can and cannot prove, and sentence 12 still calls the results "strong evidence" rather than final proof. Nothing in the draft says the results should be thrown out.$q$, 'draft', 'cb089783-aab3-5f17-8e7f-a0da3a07aa3b')
