   $q$Read the sentence: "Nadia returned the backpack to the store that had a broken zipper." Which revision is clear?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Nadia returned the backpack that had a broken zipper to the store.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Nadia returned the backpack to the store, that had a broken zipper.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-fix-for-modifier"},{"text":"That had a broken zipper, Nadia returned the backpack to the store.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"clause-moved-to-front"},{"text":"Nadia, who had a broken zipper, returned the backpack to the store.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"clause-attached-to-person"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Nadia returned the backpack that had a broken zipper to the store.$q$, $q$The clause "that had a broken zipper" describes the backpack, so it belongs right after "backpack." Adding a comma does not help, because the clause still sits next to "store."$q$, 'draft', null)
