   $q$Read the sentence: "Walking into the auditorium, the stage lights blinded Tomas." What is the problem?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Nothing is wrong, because the phrase clearly describes Tomas.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misses-dangling-modifier"},{"text":"The sentence is a fragment because it has no main verb.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misidentifies-as-fragment"},{"text":"The opening phrase seems to say the stage lights were walking.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The comma after \"auditorium\" should be taken out.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"blames-punctuation"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The opening phrase seems to say the stage lights were walking.$q$, $q$An opening phrase describes the subject that comes right after the comma, and here that subject is "the stage lights," which cannot walk. Tomas is the walker, but he is not the subject, so the phrase dangles.$q$, 'draft', null)
