   $q$Which sentence places the phrase "covered in mud" so that it clearly describes the dog?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Covered in mud, Aiyana watched the dog run through the kitchen.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opening-phrase-wrong-subject"},{"text":"Aiyana, covered in mud, watched the dog run through the kitchen.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"phrase-attached-to-person"},{"text":"Covered in mud, the dog ran through Aiyana's kitchen.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The dog ran through Aiyana's kitchen covered in mud.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"phrase-next-to-wrong-noun"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Covered in mud, the dog ran through Aiyana's kitchen.$q$, $q$When "covered in mud" opens the sentence, it describes the subject right after the comma, which is "the dog." At the end of the first sentence, it sits next to "kitchen," so the kitchen sounds muddy.$q$, 'draft', null)
